  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0375 and it contains seven tables. The first table is called Device and it has the following columns: Device_Status, ID (primary key), IP_Address, Installation_Location, Installation_Time, Name, and Type. The second table is called User and it has the following columns: ID (primary key), User_Account, and User_Password. The third table is called Staff and it has the following columns: Contact_Information, ID (primary key), and Name. The fourth table is called Network_Traffic and it has the following columns: Device_ID (foreign key referencing Device), Download_Traffic, Timestamp, Total_Traffic, Traffic_Status, Upload_Traffic, and a composite primary key (Device_ID, Timestamp). The fifth table is called Device_Failure_Record and it has the following columns: Device_ID (foreign key referencing Device), Failure_Description, Failure_Occurrence_Time, Failure_Type, Handling_Status, Remarks, and a composite primary key (Device_ID, Failure_Occurrence_Time). The sixth table is called User_Connection_Device and it has the following columns: Connection_Time, Device_ID (foreign key referencing Device), Disconnection_Time, Used_Bandwidth, User_ID (foreign key referencing User), User_IP, and a composite primary key (User_ID, Device_ID, Connection_Time). The seventh table is called Device_Maintenance_Record and it has the following columns: Device_ID (foreign key referencing Device), Maintenance_Content, Maintenance_Result, Maintenance_Time, Remarks, Staff_ID (foreign key referencing Staff), and a composite primary key (Device_ID, Staff_ID, Maintenance_Time).",
  "gold_question": "The wireless network monitoring and device management system primarily functions to manage device information, record network traffic data, track device failures and maintenance status, and monitor user connections to devices. The system is also capable of tracking maintenance operations performed by staff on the devices. The database includes the following functions:\n\nDevice Management: record basic information of all network devices. Fields include Device ID, Name, Type, IP Address, Installation Location, Installation Time, and Device Status. \n \nUser Management: store user account information. Fields include User ID, User Account, and User Password. \n \nNetwork traffic Management: record network traffic data of each device at specific time points. Fields include Device ID, Timestamp, Upload Traffic, Download Traffic, Total Traffic, and Traffic Status.  \n\nDevice failure record Management: record device failure information. Fields include Device ID, Failure Occurrence Time, Failure Type, Failure Description, Handling Status, and Remarks.  \n\nStaff Management: record information about staff members. Fields include Staff ID, Name, and Contact Information.  \n\nUser connection device Management: record the connection status between users and devices. Fields include User ID, Device ID, Connection Time, Disconnection Time, Bandwidth Used, and User IP.  \n\nDevice maintenance record Management: Used to document device maintenance information. Fields include Device ID, Staff ID, Maintenance Time, Maintenance Content, Maintenance Result, and Remarks.  \n\nThe design of thus system is primarily for device management, network traffic monitoring, failure diagnosis and handling, tracking user connection status, and maintaining device maintenance records.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0375.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0375\nCREATE TABLE `Device` (\n  `ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Device_Status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `IP_Address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Installation_Location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Installation_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `User_Account` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `User_Password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Staff` (\n  `ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Contact_Information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Network_Traffic` (\n  `Device_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Download_Traffic` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Total_Traffic` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Traffic_Status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Upload_Traffic` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Device_ID`, `Timestamp`),\n  CONSTRAINT `network_traffic_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Device_ID`) REFERENCES `Device` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Device_Failure_Record` (\n  `Device_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Failure_Occurrence_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Failure_Description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Failure_Type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Handling_Status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Device_ID`, `Failure_Occurrence_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_failure_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Device_ID`) REFERENCES `Device` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Connection_Device` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Device_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Connection_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Disconnection_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Used_Bandwidth` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `User_IP` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`, `Device_ID`, `Connection_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_connection_device_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Device_ID`) REFERENCES `Device` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Device_Maintenance_Record` (\n  `Device_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Staff_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Maintenance_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Maintenance_Content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Maintenance_Result` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Remarks` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Device_ID`, `Staff_ID`, `Maintenance_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Device_ID`) REFERENCES `Device` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `device_maintenance_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Staff_ID`) REFERENCES `Staff` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
